                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Common personal injury limits</th>
                  <td>$300K, $500K, and $1M</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Replaces home or auto insurance?</th>
                  <td>No</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Covers your own property?</th>
                  <td>Generally no</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Covers your own injuries?</th>
                  <td>Generally no</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Coverage varies by</th>
                  <td>Insurer, state, policy form, underwriting, selected limits, and underlying exposures</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <section id="final-thoughts" class="final-thoughts">
            <p class="section-label">A final word</p>
            <h3>Understanding is part of protection.</h3>
            <p>
              Most people never expect to experience a catastrophic accident or face
              a major lawsuit. These situations may be uncommon, but their financial
              consequences can be life-changing.
            </p>
            <p>
              Umbrella insurance exists to help bridge the gap between the liability
              limit of an underlying policy and the true cost of a significant covered
              claim.
            </p>
            <p>
              The goal is not to purchase more insurance than you need. The goal is to
              understand your risks, ask informed questions, and choose protection that
              aligns with your household, assets, income, and future.
            </p>
            <blockquote>
              Knowledge is one of the most valuable forms of protection you can have.
            </blockquote>
          </section>

